The original post was wrong for p = 30. If the winner reached 30, the previous state was 29 to r. Had r been 27 or lower, the winner would already have won at 29 with a lead of at least 2, so the game would have ended earlier. The loser's score must therefore be 28 or 29, not 0 to 29.

```python
def pre(p):
    return And(p >= 21, p <= 30)

def post(p, r):
    return Or(
        # Winner at 21: the game ended with a lead of at least 2, so loser has 0..19
        And(p == 21, r >= 0, r <= 19),
        # Winner at 22..29: the game was won by a 2-point lead, so loser has exactly p-2
        And(p >= 22, p <= 29, r == p - 2),
        # Winner at 30: loser has 28 or 29 (with 27 or fewer, the game would have ended at 29)
        And(p == 30, r >= 28, r <= 29)
    )
```
